P68871 — Hemoglobin Subunit Beta (HBB — Homo sapiens)
Description: The beta-globin subunit of adult human hemoglobin ($\alpha_2\beta_2$), responsible for oxygen transport from lungs to tissues.
Best for: Studying point mutations (e.g., Glu6Val in Sickle Cell Anemia), globin gene evolution, and secondary/tertiary structure sequence mapping.
